Subject: [#94-9-566] The Art of the Interface

The Inteface can be described as the boundry between two or more systems ,
as we approach the 21st Century the boundry has become the area of fusion 
and change . The boundries are becoming harder to define , between 
natural and artificial , human and machine and so on . The boundry can be 
seen to be dissapearing , in its place is connectivity , flow and 
fusion . The art of the interface is to encourage the connectitity and 
fusion , perhaps the role of the artist is to  brake the boundries .

In this age of electricity  , connectivity has become a key feature 
and in the words of Mashall McLuan 

"Electricity is Orientalising the West "

Indeed Buddhists are concerned with the art of connectivity , flow , 
change and life . Many of the questions raised by the electronic age can 
be  answered by the understanding of the Buddhist teachings .
I beleive there is a lot to be gained in the combining of the Buddhist 
way of life with the technological age .

I am currently writing a 5000 word paper on this subject and would be 
pleased to hear the opinions of others on the subject .





 

